FONTS

Two serifs are bundled, and neither is mine or covered by either licence above.
Both are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, whose full text is in `licenses/`
and must travel with any copy of the files.

They are handled differently on purpose, and the difference is the OFL's rule
about names. Literata reserves no font name, so it can be cut down and still be
called Literata. Source Serif reserves the name "Source", so a modified copy
could not be offered under the name it is offered under here — and it is
therefore bundled exactly as its authors published it, at about 450 KB more than
a cut-down copy would have cost.


LITERATA

Bundled under the OFL 1.1, full text in `licenses/Literata-OFL.txt`:

  app/src/main/res/font/literata_regular.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/literata_italic.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/literata_bold.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/literata_bold_italic.ttf

  SPDX-License-Identifier: OFL-1.1
  Copyright 2017 The Literata Project Authors
  <https://github.com/googlefonts/literata>

These four files are modified versions of the upstream release, and the OFL
requires saying so. Upstream ships two variable fonts, roman and italic, with
an optical-size and a weight axis. Each of the four here is a static instance
cut from those at `opsz` 12 — the axis default, and the value drawn for running
text — and at `wght` 400 or 700, then subset to Latin: Basic, Supplement,
Extended-A and Extended-B, general punctuation, currency, and the f-ligatures.

That is 466 KB for four faces where the two variable fonts alone are 1.8 MB.
The cost is that Literata's Greek and Cyrillic are gone; a note written in
either renders in the system font instead, because Android falls back per
glyph. Deliberate, and reversible by re-cutting from upstream.

The OFL permits this. Its restriction is on names, and Literata declares no
Reserved Font Name, so the modified files may keep the name they came with.


SOURCE SERIF 4

Bundled under the OFL 1.1, full text in `licenses/SourceSerif4-OFL.txt`:

  app/src/main/res/font/source_serif_regular.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/source_serif_italic.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/source_serif_bold.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/source_serif_bold_italic.ttf

  SPDX-License-Identifier: OFL-1.1
  Copyright 2014-2021 Adobe Systems Incorporated
  <https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-serif>

These four are byte-identical to the Regular, It, Bold and BoldIt of the plain
`Source Serif 4` family in Adobe's own 4.004 release — unmodified, and verifiably
so by checksum against that release. Not instanced and not subset, unlike the
Literata files above, because this font's name table declares `with Reserved
Font Name 'Source'`: under OFL clause 3 a Modified Version may not use a
Reserved Font Name, so subsetting it and still calling it Source Serif is not
something this licence allows.

The plain family rather than the SmText, Caption, Subhead or Display cuts, which
Adobe also ships. Those are drawn for other sizes, and a couple of them arguably
suit a phone better; the plain one is the family's own default optical size,
which is the same basis Literata was cut on.

The upstream release also ships variable fonts covering every weight in one file.
They are 2.06 MB for the pair against 892 KB for these four statics, and Compose
would need per-weight variation settings to use them.


